    <detaileddescription>
<para>Two-stage Recursive Model Index (RMI) for sorted numeric key arrays.</para>
<para>Usage: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">std::vector&lt;int64_t&gt;<sp/>keys<sp/>=<sp/>{1,<sp/>3,<sp/>7,<sp/>15,<sp/>42,<sp/>100,<sp/>...};</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">std::sort(keys.begin(),<sp/>keys.end());</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="classthemis_1_1index_1_1_learned_index_1a778cca4ad1b383de2e062f1bbdbf429c" kindref="member">LearnedIndex&lt;int64_t&gt;</ref><sp/>idx(config);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">idx.train(keys);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>pos<sp/>=<sp/>idx.lookup(42);<sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Returns<sp/>index<sp/>into<sp/>keys[]</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Or<sp/>with<sp/>a<sp/>payload<sp/>array:</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>result<sp/>=<sp/>idx.lookupKey(42,<sp/>keys);<sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Returns<sp/>optional&lt;size_t&gt;<sp/>position</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
